use std
into mold_sky.amni
dialect js

This file is a library built for the web as a wasm module; its `main()` does nothing. JavaScript drives it through its exported functions (every name starting with im_ is exported). It is a port of `simulate`, with its `pack` and `hold` phases, from cad/injmold.js, the injection-molding fill, pack and cure simulator. Results are compared bit for bit with the JavaScript simulator, so every floating-point formula keeps the JavaScript evaluation order exactly: arithmetic is f64, each sum starts at 0.0 and adds or subtracts its terms one at a time in loop order, products and quotients group left to right as written, and nothing is fused, reordered or vectorized across terms of one sum. Natural log, exp, pow and log1p always go through the externs `im_log`, `im_exp`, `im_pow` and `im_log1p`, never a Helium math function; square root and absolute value are the plain f64 operations. Wherever this file says max or min of reals it means `jmax` and `jmin`. A value "is set" when it is not NaN; NaN stands for JavaScript null. The module imports module `mold_amg` for the sparse solver; its own names (`IP`, `FP`, `LV`, `RPI`, `CII`, `VAI`, `BI`, `XI`, `AG`, `GR`, `GC`, `GV`, `GP`, `PR`, `PZ`, `PP`, `PQ`, `ipv`, `fpv`, `ip_add`, `fp_add`, `diag_of`, `aggregate`, `galerkin`, `chol`, `push_level`, `setup`, `gs`, `cyc`, `mv`, `Lv`) must not be redefined here.

```amni
import mold_amg;
extern fn im_view_f64(id i32, xs real[:]) = "im_view_f64";
extern fn im_view_i32(id i32, xs i32[:]) = "im_view_i32";
extern fn im_view_u8(id i32, xs u8[:]) = "im_view_u8";
extern fn im_log(x real) real = "im_log";
extern fn im_exp(x real) real = "im_exp";
extern fn im_pow(x real, y real) real = "im_pow";
extern fn im_log1p(x real) real = "im_log1p";
extern fn im_acos(x real) real = "im_acos";
extern fn im_onp(ph i32, a real, b real, c real) = "im_onp";
const RG real = 8.314462618;
const K0 real = 273.15;
const NZ int = 12;
const NL int = 13;
const LSN int = 4001;
var NV int = 0;
var NT int = 0;
var NK int = 0;
var NC int = 0;
var NG int = 0;
var MID int = 0;
var N1 int = 0;
var MN int = 0;
var LA i32[>..];
var LB i32[>..];
var NA0 i32[>..];
var NAL i32[>..];
var NE0 i32[>..];
var NEL i32[>..];
var EL i32[>..];
var CT real[>..];
var LE i32[>..];
var LK real[>..];
var VV real[>..];
var HE real[>..];
var AE real[>..];
var GPH real[>..];
var TT i32[>..];
var CI i32[>..];
var CJ i32[>..];
var CW real[>..];
var CC real[>..];
var HN real[>..];
var SKW real[>..];
var SKIN u8[>..];
var NRM real[>..];
var GT i32[>..];
var CF real[>..];
var MV real[>..];
var CU real[>..];
var TP real[>..];
var OUT real[>..];
var PMV real[>..];
var RNO real[>..];
var WLD i32[>..];
var WAN real[>..];
var AIR i32[>..];
var ISW u8[>..];
var GSF u8[>..];
var OKE u8[>..];
var GW real[>..];
var DW real[>..];
var BD u8[>..];
var ANG real[>..];
var CND i32[>..];
var GPK i32[>..];
var DM real[>..];
var DJ real[>..];
var LG real[>..];
var HK real[>..];
var HV i32[>..];
var GRN i32[>..];
var GRC real[>..];
var GRL real[>..];
var NP real[>..];
var NSK u8[>..];
var THI real = 0.0;
var CAPT real = 0.0;
var CAPP real = 1.0;
```

Inputs, filled by JavaScript after `im_mesh`: per link (NK links) `LA` and `LB` (the two end nodes), `LE` and `LK` (2 per link: the elements on each side, -1 when none, and their conductance shares); per node (NV nodes) `NA0` (NV+1 starts into `NAL`, the links of each node), `NE0` (NV+1 starts into `NEL`, the triangles of each node), `VV` (node volume), `HN` (node thickness), `SKIN` (1 for skin nodes); per triangle (NT triangles) `TT` (3 nodes), `EL` and `CT` (3 link ids and their coefficients), `HE` (thickness), `AE` (area), `SKW` (skin weight), `GPH` (9 per triangle: the xyz gradient of each corner's shape function), `NRM` (3 per triangle, the unit normal); per connector (NC connectors) `CI`, `CJ` (3 per connector), `CW` (3 per connector) and `CC`; `GT` (NG gate nodes, already deduplicated). `MID` is 1 for a midplane mesh. `MN` is NV (the injection node) and `N1` is NV+1.

`CF` holds the settings, already resolved by JavaScript: 0 Tm (melt temperature), 1 Tw (mold temperature), 2 hF, 3 hP, 4 rho, 5 cp, 6 al, 7 Tnf, 8 ag, 9 Teje, 10 dH, 11 lsr flag, 12 iso flag, 13 cure flag, 14 induction flag, 15 a0, 16 Q (0 when not given), 17 tinj, 18 pMax, 19 frac, 20 picTol, 21 pcgTol, 22 tmax (0 when not given), 23 vp, 24 pack flag, 25 tait flag, 26 packP, 27 packPct, 28 dtMax, 29 amgMin, 30 amg flag, 31 runner D (0 when there is no runner), 32 runner L, 33 sprue D (0 when there is no sprue), 34 sprue L, 35 clamp axis (-1 when not given), 36 Troom, 37 packT, 38 coolT, 39 holdT, 40 hold flag. A flag is 1.0 or 0.0. `MV` is the viscosity model: 0 model (0 newton, 1 power, 2 cross family, 3 cm), 1 form (1 carreau, else 0), 2 n, 3 mu, 4 m, 5 b, 6 T0, 7 tau, 8 D1, 9 D2, 10 D3, 11 A1, 12 A2, 13 eta0, 14 wlf flag, 15 wlf C1, 16 wlf T0, 17 wlf C2, 18 B, 19 Tb, 20 ag, 21 C1, 22 C2. `CU` is the cure model: 0 A1, 1 E1, 2 A2, 3 E2, 4 m, 5 n, 6 ti0, 7 Ti. `TP` is the Tait model: 0 b1m, 1 b2m, 2 b3m, 3 b4m, 4 b1s, 5 b2s, 6 b3s, 7 b4s, 8 b5, 9 b6, 10 b7, 11 b8, 12 b9.

`im_mesh(nv i32, nt i32, nk i32, nc i32, ng i32, mid i32)` stores the counts in `NV`, `NT`, `NK`, `NC`, `NG` and `MID`, sets `MN` to nv and `N1` to nv+1, sizes every input to its length filled with zeros (`CF` 64, `MV` 32, `CU` 16, `TP` 16, `PMV` 3·nv, `RNO` 3), then reports views in this order: `im_view_i32` 20 `LA`, 21 `LB`, 22 `NA0`, 23 `NAL`, 24 `NE0`, 25 `NEL`, 26 `EL`, `im_view_f64` 27 `CT`, `im_view_i32` 28 `LE`, `im_view_f64` 29 `LK`, 30 `VV`, 31 `HE`, 32 `AE`, 33 `GPH`, `im_view_i32` 34 `TT`, 35 `CI`, 36 `CJ`, `im_view_f64` 37 `CW`, 38 `CC`, 39 `HN`, 40 `SKW`, `im_view_u8` 41 `SKIN`, `im_view_f64` 42 `NRM`, `im_view_i32` 43 `GT`, `im_view_f64` 44 `CF`, 45 `MV`, 46 `CU`, 47 `TP`, 48 `PMV`, 49 `RNO`. `NAL` has 2·nk entries and `NEL` has 3·nt.

`jmax(a, b)` and `jmin(a, b)` are JavaScript's Math.max and Math.min of two reals: NaN when either is NaN, otherwise the larger or smaller. Math.min or Math.max of more values folds them left to right the same way. `hypot3(a, b, c)` is exactly V8's Math.hypot of three numbers: the absolute values are taken and mx is the largest of them (starting from 0.0, replaced when a value is larger); when mx is infinite the result is infinity; when any input is NaN the result is NaN; when mx is 0 the result is 0. Otherwise, with Kahan summation, sum and comp start at 0.0, and for each absolute value in order: q is the value divided by mx, summand is q·q minus comp, prelim is sum plus summand, comp becomes (prelim minus sum) minus summand, and sum becomes prelim. The result is the square root of sum, times mx.

Layer constants (NL entries each): `ZE`[k] is k/12. `OM`[k] is 0.5/12 for k equal to 0 or 12, else 1/12. `SW`[k] is w/36 with w equal to 1 for k equal to 0 or 12, 4 for odd k and 2 otherwise. They are module arrays built once by `lay_init()`. A layered per-node value lives at index i·NL+k, a layered per-triangle value at e·NL+k.

The fluidity model. Module real `SL` is the slope left by the last fluidity evaluation. The cross table `XT` (LSN reals) belongs to (form, n) stored in module reals `XF` and `XN` (start at NaN, so the first use builds it); `xtab()` rebuilds it only when MV's form or n differs from them. Entry i has u equal to -40 plus i·0.02 and is found by 120 bisection steps on y with lo at -400 and hi at 0: m is (lo plus hi)/2, then hi becomes m when f(m) is above 0, else lo becomes m; the entry is (lo plus hi)/2. For form 1, f(y) is y plus (1 minus n)·`im_log1p`(`im_exp`(u minus y)); otherwise f(y) is `im_exp`(y) plus `im_exp`((1 minus n)·u plus n·y), minus 1. `xlook(u) real`: q is (u plus 40)/0.02; when q is at most 0, SL becomes 0 and the result is 0; when q is at least 4000, SL becomes (1 minus n)/n and the result is XT[4000] minus (u minus (-40 plus 4000·0.02))·(1 minus n)/n; otherwise i is q truncated to an integer and f is q minus i, SL becomes -(XT[i+1] minus XT[i])/0.02 and the result is XT[i] plus (XT[i+1] minus XT[i])·f.

`fluid(T, tau, a, p) real` is the fluidity of model `MV`. Model 0: SL becomes 0, result 1/mu. Model 1: e is 1/n minus 1 and SL becomes e; mm is m·`im_exp`(-b·(T minus T0)) when b is nonzero (b times... with -b being the negated b), else m; the result is `im_pow`(tau, e)/`im_pow`(mm, 1/n) when tau is above 0, else 0 when e is above 0, else 1/mm. Models 2 and 3: TK is T plus K0, aa is a when a is above 0 else 0, ph is 1. For model 3: when aa is at least ag, SL becomes 0 and the result is 0; e0 is eta0·`im_pow`(10, -wlfC1·(T minus wlfT0)/(wlfC2 plus T minus wlfT0)) when the wlf flag is set (that is (-wlfC1)·(T minus wlfT0), divided by ((wlfC2 plus T) minus wlfT0)), else B·`im_exp`(Tb/TK); ph is `im_pow`(ag/(ag minus aa), C1 plus C2·aa). For model 2: pp is p when p is above 0 else 0, d is (TK minus D2) minus D3·pp; when d is at most 0, SL becomes 0 and the result is 0; e0 is D1·`im_exp`((-A1)·d/((A2 plus D3·pp) plus d)). Then, for both: when tau is not above 0 (NaN included), SL becomes 0 and the result is 1/(ph·e0); otherwise lx is `xlook`(`im_log`(tau/(ph·tau0))) with tau0 being MV's tau, and the result is 1/((ph·e0)·`im_exp`(lx)). `im_run` calls `xtab()` first when the model is 2 or 3.

`pipe_dp(T, Q, D, L, a) real` is the pressure drop of a round pipe: 0 when Q is not above 0, L is not above 0 or D is not above 0. R is D/2. qf(tw): s starts at 0; for i from 0 to 32 inclusive, tau is tw·i/32 and s gets wt·tau·tau·tau·`fluid`(T, tau, a, 0) added, with wt 1 for i equal to 0 or 32, 4 for odd i and 2 otherwise; qf is 3.141592653589793·`im_pow`(R, 3)/`im_pow`(tw, 3)·s·tw/96 (left to right). lo is `im_log`(1e-3) and hi is `im_log`(1e10); 90 times: m is (lo plus hi)/2, then lo becomes m when qf(`im_exp`(m)) is below Q, else hi becomes m. The result is 2·L·`im_exp`((lo plus hi)/2)/R. `dps(Q) real` is `pipe_dp`(Tm, Q, sprue D, sprue L, 0) when sprue D is above 0, else 0.

Cure and density. `kamal(TK, a) real`: k1 is A1·`im_exp`((-E1)/(RG·TK)), k2 is A2·`im_exp`((-E2)/(RG·TK)), x is a when a is above 0 else 0; 0 when x is at least 1, else (k1 plus k2·`im_pow`(x, m))·`im_pow`(1 minus x, n). `cure_step(TK, a, dt) real`: t starts at 0; while t is below dt: r is kamal(TK, a), h is min(dt minus t, 0.004/r when r is above 0 else dt), k1 is r, k2 is kamal(TK, a plus h·k1/2), k3 is kamal(TK, a plus h·k2/2), k4 is kamal(TK, a plus h·k3); a becomes min(1, a plus h·(((k1 plus 2·k2) plus 2·k3) plus k4)/6), t gets h added, and the loop stops once a is at least 1. Returns a. `induct(TK, s, dt) real` is s plus dt/(ti0·`im_exp`(Ti/TK)) when ti0 is nonzero, else 1. `tait(TK, p) real`: pp is p when above 0 else 0, Tt is b5 plus b6·pp, dT is TK minus b5, melt is TK above Tt; v0 is b1m plus b2m·dT (melt) or b1s plus b2s·dT; B is b3m·`im_exp`((-b4m)·dT) (melt) or b3s·`im_exp`((-b4s)·dT); vt is 0 (melt) or b7·`im_exp`(b8·dT minus b9·pp). Module real `DVP` becomes (-v0)·0.0894/(B plus pp) minus b9·vt, and the result is v0·(1 minus 0.0894·`im_log`(1 plus pp/B)) plus vt.

State, sized by `im_run` before anything else: per node `F` (fill fraction), `FO`, `TF` (fill time, Infinity), `TFF` (NaN), `PMX`, `GAMN`, `TAUN`, `QIN`, `CN`, `CA`, `PEND`, `PVPN`, `TEND`, `FRZE`, `ALE`, `ALM`, `VS`, `MS`, `CD`, `PNN`, `MM`, `SHR`, `SNK`, `T90` (Infinity), `AHD`, `CDG` (reals); `WET` (u8), `SEQ`, `ISG` (-1), `SO` (i32); per node and layer `TL` (Tm), `AL` (a0, lsr only), `IN` (0, induction only), `PHN` (reals); per unknown (N1) `P`, `DG`, `BB`, `RR`, `ZZ`, `DD`, `QQ` (reals) and `FULL`, `UK` (u8); per triangle `GE`, `CE`, `SLE`, `GRE`, `TWE`, `FZE`, `APZ` (reals), `ACT` (u8), `ACTL` (i32); per triangle and layer `PH`, `PHI`; per link `W`, `WGEO`; per gate `WG` (1.0), `WF`; per connector `WC`; per layer `PS`, `UU`, `TA`, `TB`, `TC`, `TD`, `NUM`, `DEN`, `ANUM`, `PRF`. vpAt starts unset (NaN). pVP, pHold, clampAt, pEndT, pInjMax, pGateMax, clampMax, pPic, Gavg, t, vfill, lost and every counter start at 0.0 or 0, never NaN. The module reals for the physical limits: THI is ((jmax(CF[0], CF[1]) plus CF[18]/(CF[4]·CF[5])) plus (CF[10]/CF[5] when CF[10] is above 0, else 0.0)) plus 1.0, formed left to right with CF[4]·CF[5] multiplied first; CAPT starts at 0.0 and CAPP at 1.0.

`pcl(x real, c real) real` clamps a pressure: when x is below c, the result is x when x is above 0.0, else 0.0; otherwise (x not below c, which includes NaN) the result is c.

`elem(e)` for triangle e with nodes a, b, c: nw is the number of them that are wet, bh is HE[e]/2, G is GE[e], pb is ((P[a] plus P[b]) plus P[c])/3; I2, Is, fz, gm and tw start at 0. For each layer k: Tk is ((x(a) plus x(b)) plus x(c))/nw when nw is nonzero, with x(n) being TL[n·NL+k] for a wet node and 0.0 otherwise, else Tm; ak is the same over AL when lsr and nw is nonzero, else 0; tau is ZE[k]·bh·G; ps is 0 with SL set to 0 when Tk is below Tnf, else `fluid`(Tk, tau, ak, pb); PS[k] is ps; z2 is ZE[k]·ZE[k]·SW[k]; I2 gets z2·ps added and Is gets z2·ps·SL added; when ps is not above 0, fz gets OM[k] added, else when tau is above tw, tw becomes tau; g is tau·ps and gm becomes g when g is above gm; PHI[e·NL+k] is tau·tau·ps. Then CE[e] is 2·bh·bh·bh·I2, SLE[e] is Is/I2 when I2 is above 0 else 0; UU[12] is 0 and for k from 11 down to 0, UU[k] is UU[k+1] plus 0.5·(ZE[k]·PS[k] plus ZE[k+1]·PS[k+1])/12; s is the sum of OM[k]·UU[k]; PH[e·NL+k] is OM[k]·UU[k]/s when s is above 0, else OM[k]; GRE[e] is gm, TWE[e] is tw, FZE[e] is fz. `elems_all()` runs elem for each active triangle in activation order (`ACTL`[0] to `ACTL`[nAct-1]).

`weights()`: W, CN and CA are zeroed. For each active triangle e in activation order with C equal to CE[e]: for c below 3, W[EL[3e+c]] gets CT[3e+c]·C added; when SKW[e] is above 0.5, for c below 3 with i equal to TT[3e+c], CN[i] gets AE[e]·C added and CA[i] gets AE[e] added. WC[q] is CC[q]·CN[i]/CA[i] when CA[i] is above 0 (i is CI[q]), else 0. Negative W become 0. mw starts at 0 and becomes max(mw, W[NAL[s]]) over every link slot s of every gate. For each gate gi: qg is max(Qset/NG·1e-3, abs(WG[gi]·(P[MN] minus P[gate]))); WG[gi] becomes qg/max(`pipe_dp`(Tm, qg, runner D, runner L), 1e-3) when runner D is above 0, else 1e3·mw when mw is above 0, else max(WG[gi], 1e-20).

`apply(x, y)` with x and y two real slices of N1 entries: y[i] is CDG[i]·x[i] when UK[i] is set, a diagonal is in use and i is below NV, else 0. Links with w equal to W[l] above 0, i equal to LA[l], j equal to LB[l]: both unknown: v is w·(x[i] minus x[j]), y[i] gets v added and y[j] gets v subtracted; only i unknown: y[i] gets w·x[i] added; only j unknown: y[j] gets w·x[j] added. Gates g with w equal to WG[g] above 0 do the same with MN as i and the gate as j. Connectors with w equal to WC[q] above 0: v is w·(((u(i) minus l0·u(j0)) minus l1·u(j1)) minus l2·u(j2)), where u(n) is x[n] when n is unknown else 0.0, i is CI[q], j0 to j2 are CJ[3q] to CJ[3q+2] and l0 to l2 are CW[3q] to CW[3q+2]; y[i] gets v added and y[j0], y[j1], y[j2] get l0·v, l1·v, l2·v subtracted.

`amg_solve() i32` assembles into `VA` (one value per pattern slot, zeroed): when a diagonal is in use, VA[DSL[i]] gets CDG[i] added for each node; each link with w above 0 adds w to slot LSL[4l], subtracts w from LSL[4l+1] and LSL[4l+2] and adds w to LSL[4l+3]; each gate with WG above 0 does the same through GSL[4g..4g+3]; each connector with w equal to WC[q] above 0 adds w·ca·cb to CSL[16q+4a+b] for a and b below 4 (in that loop order), with coefficients 1, -CW[3q], -CW[3q+1], -CW[3q+2]. Then UX[i] is the running count of unknowns before i for unknown i, else -1, and n is the unknown count; the compressed matrix keeps, for each unknown row in order, its pattern entries whose column is unknown and whose value is not exactly 0, with columns renumbered by UX, row starts in `CRP`, columns in `CCI`, values in `CVA`; `CB`[UX[i]] is BB[i] and `CX`[UX[i]] is P[i]. With k entries kept: `am_alloc`(n, k); `RPI` gets CRP[0..n], `CII` gets CCI[0..k-1], `VAI` gets CVA[0..k-1], `BI` gets CB[0..n-1], `XI` gets CX[0..n-1]; it is `am_solve`(pcgTol, 800, 160, 0.08, 1); each unknown P[i] becomes XI[UX[i]]; amgIt gets it added and amgN gets 1 added. Returns it.

`solve(mode) i32` (mode 0 for fill, 1 for pack): DG is zeroed; when a diagonal is in use, DG[i] is CDG[i] for nodes; links with w above 0 add w to DG of both ends; every gate adds WG[g] to DG[MN] and to DG of the gate; connectors with w above 0 add w to DG[CI] and w·CW·CW (left to right) to DG of each CJ. Unknowns whose DG is not above 0 become known. BB is zeroed; mode 0 adds Qset to BB[MN] when ctrl is 0; mode 1 adds CDG[i]·PNN[i] minus (MS[i] minus MM[i])/dt to BB[i] for each node (dt is the module real `DT`). Gate couplings: gate j unknown and MN known: BB[j] gets WG·P[MN] added; MN unknown and j known: BB[MN] gets WG·P[j] added. Links with w above 0: i unknown, j known and P[j] nonzero and not NaN: BB[i] gets w·P[j] added; otherwise j unknown, i known and P[i] nonzero and not NaN: BB[j] gets w·P[i] added. Connectors with w above 0: rd starts at 0 when CI is unknown, else P[CI]; for c below 3, when CJ[3q+c] is known, rd gets CW[3q+c]·P[CJ[3q+c]] subtracted; skip when rd is 0 or NaN; when CI is unknown BB[CI] gets w·rd subtracted; each unknown CJ[3q+c] gets CW[3q+c]·w·rd added. When the unknown count is at least amgMin and the amg flag is set, return `amg_solve()`. Otherwise run conjugate gradients on P with up to 30000 iterations: `apply`(P, QQ); for each unknown i: RR[i] is BB[i] minus QQ[i], ZZ[i] is RR[i]/DG[i], DD[i] is ZZ[i], rz gets RR[i]·ZZ[i] added and bn gets BB[i]·BB[i] added; known entries of RR, ZZ and DD are 0. bn becomes its square root; when bn is not above 0, every unknown P becomes 0 and the result is 0. Each iteration: rn is the sum over unknowns of RR·RR; stop when the square root of rn is at most pcgTol·bn; `apply`(DD, QQ); dq is the sum over unknowns of DD·QQ; al is rz/dq; rz2 starts at 0 and for each unknown P gets al·DD added, RR gets al·QQ subtracted, ZZ becomes RR/DG and rz2 gets RR·ZZ added; be is rz2/rz, rz becomes rz2, and each unknown DD becomes ZZ plus be·DD. Returns the iteration count.

`grad_at(e) real`: gx, gy and gz start at 0; for c below 3 with pc equal to P[TT[3e+c]], they get pc·GPH[9e+3c], pc·GPH[9e+3c+1] and pc·GPH[9e+3c+2] added; the result is `hypot3`(gx, gy, gz). `conduct(i, dt, hh, src)` with src 1 meaning PHN is the heat source: bh is HN[i]/2, dz is bh/12, r is al·dt/(dz·dz), be is 2·dt·hh/(rho·cp·dz), o is i·NL; for each layer TA[k] is -r, TB[k] is 1 plus 2·r, TC[k] is -r and TD[k] is TL[o+k] plus (PHN[o+k]·dt/(rho·cp) when src is 1, else 0.0); TC[0] becomes -2·r, TA[12] becomes -2·r, TB[12] gets be added and TD[12] gets be·Tw added; for k from 1 to 12: m is TA[k]/TB[k-1], TB[k] gets m·TC[k-1] subtracted and TD[k] gets m·TD[k-1] subtracted; TL[o+12] is TD[12]/TB[12], and for k from 11 down to 0, TL[o+k] is (TD[k] minus TC[k]·TL[o+k+1])/TB[k]. `cure(i, dt)` does nothing unless lsr and the cure flag are set; for each layer with TK equal to TL[o+k] plus K0: when the induction flag is set and IN[o+k] is below 1, IN[o+k] becomes `induct`(TK, IN[o+k], dt) and the layer is skipped while it stays below 1; then a0 is AL[o+k], a1 is `cure_step`(TK, a0, dt), AL[o+k] becomes a1 and, when dH is nonzero, TL[o+k] gets dH·(a1 minus a0)/cp added. `bulk(i) real` is the sum of OM[k]·TL[i·NL+k]. `frz_of(i) real` is the sum of OM[k] over layers where (lsr: AL is at least ag; otherwise TL is below Tnf). `alm(i) real` is the sum of OM[k]·AL[i·NL+k].

`link_prof(l)` fills `PRF`: e0 is LE[2l], e1 is LE[2l+1]; c0 is max(0, LK[2l])·CE[e0]·ACT[e0] when e0 is at least 0, else 0; c1 likewise with e1 and LK[2l+1]; s is c0 plus c1; PRF[k] is ((c0·PH[e0·NL+k] when c0 is nonzero, else 0.0) plus (c1·PH[e1·NL+k] when c1 is nonzero, else 0.0))/s when s is above 0, else OM[k]. `activate(i)`: for each triangle e in node i's list (NEL from NE0[i] to NE0[i+1]) that is not active: it becomes active and is appended to ACTL (nAct grows); g and n start at 0; for each of e's three nodes j and each triangle e2 in j's list that is active, is not e and has GE[e2] above 0, g gets `im_log`(GE[e2]) added and n grows by 1; GE[e] is `im_exp`(g/n) when n is nonzero, else Gavg when Gavg is above 0, else 1e7.

Connector visits. `CM0` (NV+1 starts) and `CMQ` list, for each node in connector order, the connector touches: a connector q adds 4q+3 to the list of CI[q] and then 4q+c to the list of CJ[3q+c] for c below 3, counted first and filled in that order. `cin(i, dt, mode)` goes over node i's touches in list order: q is the touch divided by 4 and c its remainder; skip when WC[q] (w) is not above 0; r is P[CI[q]] minus CW[3q]·P[CJ[3q]] minus CW[3q+1]·P[CJ[3q+1]] minus CW[3q+2]·P[CJ[3q+2]] (one at a time). For c equal to 3 with r below 0: Q is (-w)·r·dt and each wet CJ[3q+k] j is visited with Q·CW[3q+k]. For c below 3 with r above 0 and CI[q] wet: CI[q] is visited with w·r·dt·CW[3q+c]. A visit of node j with amount Q in mode 0: for each layer, qk is Q·OM[k], NUM[k] gets qk·TL[j·NL+k] added, DEN[k] gets qk added and, when lsr, ANUM[k] gets qk·AL[j·NL+k] added. In mode 1: module reals QS gets Q added, QB gets Q·`bulk`(j) added and, when lsr, QA gets Q·`alm`(j) added.

`thermal(dt)` does nothing when iso. The wet nodes in ascending order go into SO (nw of them) and are stably sorted (merge sort; equal entries keep their order) so that node a comes before node b when P[a] is above P[b], or when P[a] equals P[b] and SEQ[a] is below SEQ[b]. PHN is zeroed and a fresh per-node real array aw is zeroed; for each active triangle e in activation order, wa is AE[e]·SKW[e], and for its three nodes i, aw[i] gets wa added and PHN[i·NL+k] gets wa·PHI[e·NL+k] added for each layer; every node with aw above 0 has its PHN layers divided by aw. Then each node i of SO in order, with o equal to i·NL, f0 equal to FO[i] and cap equal to VV[i]·f0: When f0 is at least 1 minus 1e-12: NUM[k] is cap·OM[k]·TL[o+k], DEN[k] is cap·OM[k] and, when lsr, ANUM[k] is cap·OM[k]·AL[o+k]; for each link l of i (NAL from NA0[i] to NA0[i+1]) with w equal to W[l] above 0, j the other end and dp equal to P[j] minus P[i] above 0: Q is w·dp·dt, the profile pf is `link_prof`(l) (PRF) when LE[2l] is at least 0, else OM, and for each layer qk is Q·pf[k], NUM[k] gets qk·TL[j·NL+k] added, DEN[k] gets qk added and, when lsr, ANUM[k] gets qk·AL[j·NL+k] added; then `cin`(i, dt, 0); when i is a gate (ISG[i] at least 0), Q is WG[ISG[i]]·(P[MN] minus P[i])·dt and when Q is above 0 each layer's NUM gets Q·OM[k]·Tm added and DEN gets Q·OM[k] added; finally each layer with DEN above 0 gets TL[o+k] equal to NUM/DEN and, when lsr, AL[o+k] equal to ANUM/DEN. Otherwise QS, QB and QA start at 0; for each link of i with w above 0, dp above 0 and j wet: Q is w·dp·dt, pf as above, tb2 is the sum of pf[k]·TL[j·NL+k] and ab the sum of pf[k]·AL[j·NL+k] (0 unless lsr); QS gets Q added, QB gets Q·tb2 added and QA gets Q·ab added; then `cin`(i, dt, 1); a gate with Q (as above) above 0 adds Q to QS and Q·Tm to QB; then each overflow record with destination i, in record order, with source sx and volume vol, adds vol to QS, vol·`bulk`(sx) to QB and, when lsr, vol·`alm`(sx) to QA; when QS is above 0, each layer TL[o+k] becomes (cap·TL[o+k] plus QB)/(cap plus QS) and, when lsr, AL[o+k] becomes (cap·AL[o+k] plus QA)/(cap plus QS). After all nodes, each node of SO in order gets `conduct`(i, dt, hF, 1) and then `cure`(i, dt). Then for each node i of SO in order and each layer slot k from i·NL while k is below i·NL+NL: when TL[k] is not at most THI (this includes NaN), TL[k] becomes THI when TL[k] is above THI, else Tm, and CAPT gets 1.0 added.

`qsel(a, n, k) real` works in place on the real array a: l is 0 and r is n-1; while l is below r: x is a[(l+r)/2 rounded down], i is l, j is r; while i is at most j: while a[i] is below x, i grows; while a[j] is above x, j shrinks; when i is at most j, a[i] and a[j] swap, i grows and j shrinks. Then when k is at most j, r becomes j; else when k is at least i, l becomes i; else stop. The result is a[k].

Setup inside `im_run() i32`: it calls `lay_init()`, then calls `xtab()` when MV[0] is 2 or 3, then sizes the state; then: Vt is the sum of VV. Qset is CF[16] when it is nonzero, else Vt/tinj. tMax is CF[22] when it is nonzero, else max(20, 30·Vt/Qset). ISG[GT[g]] is g. Pressure areas: pr0, pr1, pr2 start at 0 and for each triangle e and k below 3, pr[k] gets AE[e]·abs(NRM[3e+k]) added; cax is CF[35] when it is at least 0, else 2 when pr2 is at least pr0 and at least pr1, else 1 when pr1 is at least pr0, else 0; APZ[e] is AE[e]·abs(NRM[3e+cax]) when MID is 1, else AE[e]·max(0, NRM[3e+cax]). The connector touch lists are built. The pattern of the N1×N1 matrix: row i holds i itself, the other end of each link touching i, every node among (CI[q], CJ[3q], CJ[3q+1], CJ[3q+2]) of each connector touching i, MN for each gate row and every gate in row MN; columns sorted ascending without repeats, row starts in `RP` (i32) and columns in `RC` (i32). `slot(i, j)` finds j in row i by binary search. DSL[i] is slot(i, i); LSL[4l..4l+3] are slot(i,i), slot(i,j), slot(j,i), slot(j,j) for link ends i and j; GSL[4g..4g+3] the same with MN and the gate; CSL[16q+4a+b] is slot(m[a], m[b]) for m equal to (CI[q], CJ[3q], CJ[3q+1], CJ[3q+2]). WGEO[l] is max(0, LK[2l] plus LK[2l+1]). The progress callback gets `im_onp`(3, 0, 0, 0).

Fill loop of `im_run`, while nfull is below NV:
1. steps grows by 1. UK[i] is FULL[i] for nodes. No diagonal is in use.
2. When vpAt is not yet set, vfill is at least vp·Vt and nfull is nonzero: vpAt becomes t, pVP becomes pEndT, PVPN becomes a copy of the node pressures and is marked set, pHold becomes (CF[26] when it is set, else packPct·pVP) when the pack flag is set, not lsr, the tait flag is set and not iso, else min(pVP, pMax); ctrl becomes 2.
3. sw and Qtot start at 0. Control loop: UK[MN] is 1 when ctrl is 0, else 0; when ctrl is nonzero, P[MN] becomes max(0, (pHold when ctrl is 2, else pMax) minus `dps`(min(Qset, Qtot when it is nonzero and not NaN, else Qset))). Up to 12 Picard rounds: `elems_all()`, `weights()`, its gets `solve`(0) added, pics grows by 1; ch, cw, gs and amx start at 0; for each active triangle e in activation order: g1 is max(`grad_at`(e), 1), g0 is GE[e], a is SLE[e], gn is `im_exp`((`im_log`(g1) plus a·`im_log`(g0))/(1 plus a)) when g0 is above 0, else g1, wq is AE[e]·CE[e]; amx becomes a when a is above amx; ch gets wq·abs(a·`im_log`(gn/gd)) added, with gd being g0 when g0 is nonzero and not NaN, else gn; cw gets wq added; GE[e] becomes gn; gs gets `im_log`(gn) added. When nAct is nonzero, Gavg is `im_exp`(gs/nAct). pm is P[MN]; when amx is 0, or (ch/cw when cw is above 0, else 0) is below picTol and abs(pm minus pPic) is at most picTol·0.1·abs(pm), pPic becomes pm and the rounds stop; otherwise pPic becomes pm. Then Qtot is the sum over gates of WG[g]·(P[MN] minus P[GT[g]]) and pinj is P[MN] plus `dps`(Qtot). Then: ctrl 0 with pinj above pMax and sw below 3: ctrl becomes 1, sw grows, repeat the control loop; ctrl 1 with Qtot above Qset·1.0001 and sw below 3: ctrl becomes 0, sw grows, repeat; ctrl 2 with Qtot above Qset·1.0001: ctrl becomes 0, vpAt becomes Infinity, repeat. Otherwise leave the control loop.
4. QIN is zeroed. Links with w above 0: when i is full and j is not, QIN[j] gets w·(P[i] minus P[j]) added; else when j is full and i is not, QIN[i] gets w·(P[j] minus P[i]) added. Each gate j that is not full gets WG[g]·(P[MN] minus P[j]) added. Connectors with w above 0: r is P[CI] minus the CW-weighted CJ pressures one at a time, v is w·r; an unfilled CI gets v subtracted and each unfilled CJ gets CW·v added. When ctrl is 0: qs is the sum of positive QIN over unfilled nodes, and when qs is above 0 each such QIN is multiplied by Qset/qs.
5. The front: unfilled nodes in ascending order with QIN above Qtot·1e-12 and above 0 go into growable `FL` (i32) with time VV[i]·(1 minus F[i])/QIN[i] in growable `TLS` (real).
6. pinj is P[MN] plus `dps`(Qtot); pg is the sum of the gate pressures divided by NG; pInjMax becomes max(pInjMax, pinj) and pGateMax max(pGateMax, pg); pc is P[MN]; cl starts at 0 and for each active triangle e in activation order, with a, b and c the pressures P[TT[3e]], P[TT[3e+1]] and P[TT[3e+2]]: when pc is above 1e5, CAPP becomes jmax(jmax(jmax(CAPP, a/pc), b/pc), c/pc); then cl gets APZ[e]·((`pcl`(a, pc) plus `pcl`(b, pc)) plus `pcl`(c, pc))/3 added; when cl is above clampMax, clampMax becomes cl and clampAt becomes t. Append t, pinj, pg, Qtot, vfill/Vt and cl to the growable histories `HT`, `HP`, `HG`, `HQ`, `HF`, `HC`; fz is 0, or when not iso the sum over wet nodes of VV[i]·`frz_of`(i); append fz/Vt to `HZ`. pEndT becomes pinj.
7. Stop the fill loop with a short code: 1 when the front is empty and nfull is nonzero, 2 when it is empty and nfull is 0; 3 when Qtot is below Qset·1e-5; 4 when t is at least tMax.
8. A copy of TLS is selected: kk is max(1, ceil(frac·count)) minus 1 and dt is `qsel`(copy, count, min(kk, count minus 1)); tmn is the smallest TLS entry (starting at Infinity, replaced when smaller); dt becomes max(tmn, min(min(min(dt, dtMax), (Vt minus vfill)/Qtot·1.000001), (tMax minus t) plus 1e-9)).
9. FO becomes a copy of F. The overflow records (growable `OVS` i32, `OVD` i32, `OVV` real) and the queue (growable `QUI` i32 and `QUX` real) are emptied; sq is 1.
10. For each front node i in order: add is QIN[i]·dt, rem is VV[i]·(1 minus F[i]); WET[i] is 1 and SEQ[i] is 0; when add is at least rem·(1 minus 1e-12): TF[i] is t plus min(dt, rem/QIN[i]), F[i] is 1, FULL[i] is 1, nfull grows and (i, add minus rem) is queued; otherwise F[i] gets add/VV[i] added.
11. pool starts at 0. The queue is processed in order while it grows: entry (i, ex) is skipped when ex is not above Vt·1e-14; sw2 is the sum of WGEO[l] over links of i whose other end j is not full; when sw2 is not above 0, pool gets ex added; otherwise for each link of i in order whose other end j is not full (checked at that moment) and whose WGEO is above 0: vol is ex·WGEO[l]/sw2, the record (i, j, vol) is appended, WET[j] is 1, SEQ[j] is sq and sq grows, F[j] gets vol/VV[j] added, and when F[j] is at least 1 minus 1e-12: (j, (F[j] minus 1)·VV[j]) is queued, F[j] is 1, FULL[j] is 1, nfull grows and TF[j] is t plus dt.
12. When pool is above 0: qs is the sum of QIN over front nodes that are not full; when qs is above 0, each front node i in order is handled like this: when i is not full, F[i] becomes min(1, F[i] plus pool·QIN[i]/qs/VV[i]) and, when F[i] is at least 1 minus 1e-12, F[i] is 1, FULL[i] is 1, nfull grows and TF[i] is t plus dt; when i is already full, lost gets pool added (once for each such node). When qs is not above 0, nothing happens and pool is dropped.
13. The overflow records are grouped by destination (node starts `OVC` with NV+1 entries and record numbers `OVR`, each group in record order) for `thermal`; then `thermal`(dt) and t gets dt added.
14. Each node that is full and has FO below 1 minus 1e-12 gets TFF[i] equal to TL[i·NL] and is activated.
15. For each active triangle e and its nodes i: GAMN[i] becomes GRE[e] when that is above it and TAUN[i] becomes TWE[e] when that is above it. PMX[i] becomes P[i] when that is above it.
16. vfill is the sum of VV[i]·F[i]. When vfill is at least Vt·(1 minus 1e-11), every node that is not full gets F 1, FULL 1 (nfull grows), WET 1, TF equal to t and TFF equal to TL[i·NL].
17. When steps is a multiple of 4: `im_onp`(0, vfill/Vt, t, pinj).
After the loop, when there is no short code: append t, the last HP, the last HG, 0, 1, the last HC and the last HZ to the seven histories.

Results of the fill, written by `im_run` after the loop: tFill is t; PEND is a copy of the node pressures; PVPN becomes that copy too when it was never set; TEND[i] is `bulk`(i) when wet, else NaN; FRZE[i] is `frz_of`(i) when wet, else 0; when lsr, ALE[i] is the max over layers of AL starting from 0 (max(mx, AL) each time) and ALM[i] is `alm`(i). Then, when there is no short code, not iso, the pack flag and the tait flag are set and not lsr, `pack()` runs; when there is no short code, not iso, lsr, the cure flag and the hold flag are set, `hold()` runs. `OUT` (64 reals) gets: 0 vpAt (NaN when never set or Infinity), 1 pVP, 2 pHold, 3 short code, 4 vfill/Vt, 5 tFill, 6 pEndT, 7 pInjMax, 8 pGateMax, 9 clampMax, 10 clampAt, 11 Qset, 12 Vt, 13 steps, 14 pics, 15 its, 16 lost, 17 ctrl, 18 cax, 19 amgN, 20 amgIt, 22 1 when pack ran, 23 1 when hold ran, 39 CAPT, 40 CAPP, and the pack and hold values below. Finally it reports `im_view_f64` 50 `OUT`, 51 `TF`, 52 `PEND`, 53 `PVPN`, 54 `PMX`, 55 `TFF`, 56 `TEND`, 57 `GAMN`, 58 `TAUN`, 59 `FRZE`, 60 `ALE`, 61 `ALM`, 62 `HT`, 63 `HP`, 64 `HG`, 65 `HQ`, 66 `HF`, 67 `HC`, 68 `HZ`, 69 `SHR`, 70 `SNK`, 71 `KT`, 72 `KP`, 73 `KG`, 74 `KC`, 75 `KZ`, 76 `AHD`, 77 `T90`, 78 `UT`, 79 `UA`, 80 `UM`, and returns 0. The histories are reported only after they stop growing.

`pack()`: pk is CF[26] when it is set, else pHold when pHold is nonzero and not NaN, else 0.8·pEndT; tpk is CF[37], tco is CF[38]; vr is `tait`(Troom plus K0, 0). Negative node pressures become 0. `mass(i, pp)`: mm, c and vs start at 0; per layer vv is `tait`(TL[i·NL+k] plus K0, pp), mm gets OM[k]/vv added, c gets OM[k]·DVP/(vv·vv) subtracted and vs gets OM[k]·vv added; VS[i] becomes vs and the module reals O0 and O1 become mm·VV[i] and c·VV[i]. `mw0(i, pp) real` is (the sum of OM[k]/`tait`(TL[i·NL+k] plus K0, pp))·VV[i]. `mwp(i, pp) real` is mw0(i, pp) when pp is at least 0, else a plus pp·(mw0(i, 1e5) minus a)/1e5 with a equal to mw0(i, 0). `inv(i, g) real`: mt is MM[i] and a is mw0(i, 0); when a is at least mt the result is (mt minus a)/((mw0(i, 1e5) minus a)/1e5); lo is 0 and hi is max(g, 1e6); hi doubles while mwp(i, hi) is below mt and hi is below 4e9; when hi is at least 4e9 the result is hi; x is min(max(g, lo), hi); up to 40 times: f is mwp(i, x) minus mt, stop when abs(f) is at most 1e-9·mt; hi becomes x when f is above 0, else lo becomes x; d is max(1e3, 1e-4·x); sl is (mwp(i, x plus d) minus mwp(i, x))/d; xn is x minus f/sl when sl is above 0, else NaN; x becomes xn when xn is above lo and below hi, else (lo plus hi)/2; stop when hi minus lo is below 1e-6·hi. The result is x. First, for each node, `mass`(i, P[i]) and MM[i] becomes O0.

The pack loop: WF is a copy of WG; tt is tFill; dt is min(0.02, max(1e-3, tFill/20)); gateFz, packEnd and eject are unset (NaN); minj, W0 and n2 are 0; cmax is clampMax. While n2 is below 2000: n2 grows; inPack is packEnd not being set; each node gets `conduct`(i, dt, hP when inPack else hP/2, 0). Each active triangle gets GE[e] equal to max(`grad_at`(e), 1); `elems_all()`; `weights()`; each W[l] above 0 is multiplied by 2/(VS[LA[l]] plus VS[LB[l]]); each WC[q] is divided by VS[CI[q]]; vm is `tait`(Tm plus K0, pk); each gate g gets WG[g] equal to, when inPack, WF[g]/vm when runner D is above 0, else 30·(the max of 0 and W over the gate's link slots); and 0 when not inPack. gw is the sum of W[NAL[s]] over the link slots of every gate, taken now; when W0 is 0 it becomes gw. For each node: `mass`(i, max(0, P[i])); O0 becomes mwp(i, P[i]); MS[i] is O0; dp is max(1e6, 0.1·P[i]); CD[i] is max(O1, (mwp(i, P[i] plus dp) minus O0)/dp); PNN[i] is P[i]. Then CDG[i] is CD[i]/dt and the diagonal is in use; UK[MN] is 0 and P[MN] is pk when inPack, else 0; every node is unknown; the module real `DT` is dt; `solve`(1); the diagonal is no longer in use. m0 is the sum of MM (from 0); each unknown node gets MM[i] equal to MS[i] plus CD[i]·(P[i] minus PNN[i]); links with w above 0: q is w·(P[i] minus P[j])·dt, a known i gets q subtracted from MM and a known j gets q added; connectors with w above 0: r as in the fill, f is w·r·dt, a known CI gets f subtracted and each known CJ gets CW·f added; minj gets (the sum of MM from 0) minus m0 added. Every node gets P[i] equal to `inv`(i, P[i]); tt gets dt added. fz is the sum of VV[i]·`frz_of`(i); fe is the sum of ok·VV[i], with ok 0 when some layer of node i has TL above Teje, else 1; pg is the sum over gates of max(0, P[gate]) divided by NG; cl is the sum over all triangles of APZ[e]·((`pcl`(P[a], CF[18]) plus `pcl`(P[b], CF[18])) plus `pcl`(P[c], CF[18]))/3; cmax becomes max(cmax, cl); PMX updates as in the fill. Append tt, P[MN], pg, cl and fz/Vt to `KT`, `KP`, `KG`, `KC`, `KZ`. When gateFz is unset: gf is min over gates of `frz_of`, starting at 1; when gf is at least 0.99 or gw is below 1e-4·W0, gateFz becomes tt. When inPack and (tpk is set: tt is at least tFill plus tpk; tpk unset: gateFz is set and tt is at least max(gateFz, tFill plus 0.5), or tt is at least tFill plus 30): packEnd becomes tt and `sink_of()` runs. When not inPack and (tco is set: tt is at least packEnd plus tco; unset: fe is at least Vt·0.999 or tt is at least packEnd plus 120): eject becomes tt and the loop stops. dt becomes min(dt·1.15, max(0.02, (tpk when set, else 5)/30) when inPack, else 0.5). When n2 is a multiple of 10, `im_onp`(1, 0, tt, 0). After the loop: SHR[i] is 1 minus MM[i]·vr/VV[i]; sa gets SHR[i]·VV[i] added, sv gets VV[i] added, and smax becomes max(smax, SHR[i]) for skin nodes (every node when MID is 1), smax starting at 0. OUT gets 24 pk, 25 gateFz, 26 packEnd, 27 eject, 28 eject minus packEnd when both are set (else NaN), 29 minj, 30 the sum of MM from 0, 31 sa/sv, 32 smax, 33 cmax, 34 vr, 35 1 when the sink was computed.

`sink_of()`: Tt is b5; for each node, d starts at 0 and for each layer with T equal to TL[i·NL+k] plus K0 above Tt plus b6·P[i], d gets OM[k]·(1 minus vr/`tait`(T, P[i])) added; SNK[i] is HN[i]/2·d; skin nodes (every node when MID is 1) contribute the pair (SNK[i], VV[i]) in node order. The pairs are stably sorted by the first value ascending (merge sort). tot is the sum of the volumes in sorted order; acc starts at 0 and med at 0; going through the sorted pairs, acc gets the volume added and when acc is at least tot/2, med is that pair's value and the scan stops. Each SNK[i] becomes max(0, SNK[i] minus med).

`hold()`: th is CF[39]; tt is tFill, dt is 0.05; for n from 0 while n is below 4000: each node gets `conduct`(i, dt, hF, 0) and then `cure`(i, dt); tt gets dt added; amin is 1 and am is 0; for each node, mn is min over layers of AL starting at 1; when mn is at least 0.9 and T90[i] is Infinity, T90[i] becomes tt; amin becomes min(amin, mn); am gets `alm`(i)·VV[i] added. Append tt, amin and am/Vt to `UT`, `UA`, `UM`. Stop when (th set: tt is at least tFill plus th; unset: amin is at least 0.9 or tt is at least tFill plus 600). dt becomes min(min(dt·1.1, 0.5), max(0.01, th/40) when th is set, else 0.5). When n is a multiple of 10, `im_onp`(2, 0, tt, 0). After: AHD[i] is min over layers of AL starting at 1. t90max starts at NaN and for each node in order becomes T90[i] when T90[i] is finite and not below the current value (a NaN current value is replaced). OUT gets 36 tt, 37 tt minus tFill, 38 t90max.

Helpers for JavaScript, all exported. `im_mat()` calls `xtab()` when MV's model is 2 or 3. `im_eta(T real, gd real, a real, p real) real` is the viscosity at shear rate gd: lo is -20.0 and hi is 30.0; 200 times: m is (lo plus hi)/2, tau is `im_exp`(m) and ps is `fluid`(T, tau, a, p), then lo becomes m when ps is above 0 and tau·ps is below gd, else hi becomes m. After the loop tau is `im_exp`((lo plus hi)/2) and ps is `fluid`(T, tau, a, p); the result is 1/ps when ps is above 0, else infinity. `im_pipe(T real, Q real, D real, L real, a real) real` is `pipe_dp`(T, Q, D, L, a). `im_kamal(TK real, a real) real` is `kamal`(TK, a), `im_cure(TK real, a real, dt real) real` is `cure_step`(TK, a, dt) and `im_induct(TK real, s real, dt real) real` is `induct`(TK, s, dt). `im_tait(TK real, p real) real` is `tait`(TK, p). `im_runner(W real, L real, tm real) real` sizes a runner: dp is `hsqrt`(`jmax`(W, 0.01))·`im_pow`(L, 0.25)/3.7 (left to right), dt is tm plus 1.5, D is `jmin`(12, `jmax`(3, `jmax`(dp, dt))); RNO[0] becomes dp, RNO[1] becomes dt and RNO[2] becomes `jround`(D·2)/2. `jround(x real) real` is JavaScript's Math.round: NaN stays NaN; otherwise f is `floor`(x) and the result is f plus 1 when x minus f is at least 0.5, else f. `im_runner` returns RNO[2].

Nearest node. `im_nsz(nv i32)` sizes `NP` to 3·nv reals and `NSK` to nv entries, zero-filled, and reports views `im_view_f64` 88 `NP` and `im_view_u8` 89 `NSK`. `im_near(nv i32, x real, y real, z real, only i32) i32`: best is -1 and bd is infinity; for each node i below nv, skipped when only is 1 and NSK[i] is 0: dx is NP[3i] minus x, dy is NP[3i+1] minus y, dz is NP[3i+2] minus z, and d is (dx·dx plus dy·dy) plus dz·dz; when d is below bd, bd becomes d and best becomes i. Returns best.

Welds, `im_post()`, exported; JavaScript runs it after `im_run` once it has filled `PMV` (3 per node: the midsurface node positions). `skn(i int) bool` is true when MID is 1 or SKIN[i] is nonzero; a value is finite when it is neither NaN nor infinite. `GSF` (NV entries, zeros) gets 1 at every gate node in `GT`. Per triangle e in order: f is true when TF of all three corners TT[3e], TT[3e+1] and TT[3e+2] is finite; `OKE`[e] (NT entries) is 1 when f is true and SKW[e] is above 0.5, else 0; the three entries `GW`[3e+k] (3·NT reals) start at 0.0 and, when f is true, for each corner c from 0 to 2 in order with i being TT[3e+c], GW[3e+k] gets TF[i]·GPH[9e+3c+k] added for k from 0 to 2; l is `hypot3`(GW[3e], GW[3e+1], GW[3e+2]); when l is above 0 the three are each divided by l, otherwise OKE[e] becomes 0. tmax starts at 0.0; for each node i in order: tmax becomes `jmax`(tmax, TF[i]) when TF[i] is finite, and `BD`[i] (NV entries) is 1 when some s from NE0[i] below NE0[i+1] has SKW[NEL[s]] not above 0.5 (NaN is not above), else 0. `usen(i int, tmax real) bool` is true when GSF[i] is 0, `skn`(i) holds, BD[i] is 0, TF[i] is finite and TF[i] is at least 0.02·tmax. `DW` (3·NV reals) starts at 0.0; for each triangle e in order with OKE[e] equal to 1, for each corner c in order with i being TT[3e+c], DW[3i+k] gets AE[e]·GW[3e+k] added for k from 0 to 2. Then for each node i, l is `hypot3`(DW[3i], DW[3i+1], DW[3i+2]) and when l is above 0 those three are each divided by l. `ANG` (NV reals) starts at 0.0; for each link l below NK in order, with a being LA[l] and b being LB[l], skipped unless `usen`(a, tmax) and `usen`(b, tmax): ua, ub and d start at 0.0, and for k from 0 to 2 in order, x is PMV[3b+k] minus PMV[3a+k], ua gets x·DW[3a+k] added, ub gets x·DW[3b+k] subtracted and d gets DW[3a+k]·DW[3b+k] added; when ua is above 0, ub is above 0 and d is below 0.7071067811865476, g is `im_acos`(`jmax`(-1, d))·180/3.141592653589793 (left to right), ANG[a] becomes `jmax`(ANG[a], g) and then ANG[b] becomes `jmax`(ANG[b], g). Room for growth: on the web a growable array that is not empty cannot grow past its `cap`, so each `reserve` named in these blocks is a call made right after the array is emptied and before anything is appended. `WLD` and `WAN` are emptied and each then gets `reserve`(NV), and `ISW` is sized to NV entries, zero-filled; for each node i in order with ANG[i] above 0, i is appended to WLD, ANG[i] is appended to WAN and ISW[i] becomes 1.

Air traps, the rest of `im_post()`. `CND` is emptied and then gets `reserve`(NV); for each node i in order, skipped when GSF[i] is 1, `skn`(i) is false or TF[i] is not finite: mx is true and deg is 0; for each s from NA0[i] below NA0[i+1]: l is NAL[s] and j is LB[l] when LA[l] is i, else LA[l]; j is skipped when `skn`(j) is false or TF[j] is not finite; otherwise deg grows by 1, mx becomes false when TF[j] is above TF[i], and then s3 runs from NA0[j] while s3 is below NA0[j+1] and mx is still true: l3 is NAL[s3], q is LB[l3] when LA[l3] is j, else LA[l3], and mx becomes false when `skn`(q) holds, TF[q] is finite and TF[q] is above TF[i]. When mx is true and deg is above 0, i is appended to CND. CND is then put in order of TF descending with `stable_sort`, so nodes with equal TF keep their order. el starts at 0.0 and gets `hsqrt`(AE[e]) added for each triangle e in order, then el becomes el/NT·2 (left to right). `AIR` is emptied and then gets `reserve`(50); for each i of CND in order: i is skipped when some j already in AIR has `hypot3`(PMV[3i] minus PMV[3j], PMV[3i+1] minus PMV[3j+1], PMV[3i+2] minus PMV[3j+2]) below 3·el; otherwise i is appended to AIR, and the scan stops as soon as AIR holds 50 nodes. Last, `im_post` reports views `im_view_i32` 81 `WLD`, `im_view_f64` 82 `WAN`, `im_view_i32` 83 `AIR` and `im_view_u8` 84 `ISW`.

Gate candidates, `im_gates(nc i32) i32`, exported; it reads `PMV`, `HN`, `SKIN`, `LA`, `LB`, `NA0` and `NAL`. `okn(i int) bool` is true when MID is 1 or SKIN[i] is nonzero. `pos3(c int, k int) real` is PMV[3c+k] when c is at least 0, else NaN. c0, c1 and c2 start at 0.0 and n at 0; for each node i in order with `okn`(i), `pos3`(i, k) is added to ck for k 0, 1 and 2 and n grows by 1; then each ck is divided by n as a real. first is -1 and bd is infinity; for each node i in order with `okn`(i): dx is `pos3`(i, 0) minus c0, dy is `pos3`(i, 1) minus c1, dz is `pos3`(i, 2) minus c2, d is (dx·dx plus dy·dy) plus dz·dz, and when d is below bd, bd becomes d and first becomes i. The picks `GPK` are emptied and then get `reserve`(nc); `DM` (NV reals) is filled with infinity; cur is first; for s from 0 below nc: cur is appended to GPK; far is -1 and fd is -1.0; for each node i in order with `okn`(i): dx is `pos3`(i, 0) minus `pos3`(cur, 0), dy and dz likewise for 1 and 2, d is (dx·dx plus dy·dy) plus dz·dz; DM[i] becomes d when d is below DM[i]; when DM[i] is above fd, fd becomes DM[i] and far becomes i; then cur becomes far, and the loop stops when far is -1.

Then a row per pick, in pick order, with src being the pick. When src is -1 the row is node -1, ecc 0.0 and len 0.0. Otherwise `DJ` and `LG` (NV reals) are filled with infinity, DJ[src] and LG[src] become 0.0, and the heap (keys `HK`, reals, and values `HV`, both emptied and then each given `reserve`(2·NK plus NV plus 7)) gets key 0.0 with value src pushed. `hpush(k real, v int)`: k is appended to HK and v to HV and i is the last index; while i is above 0: pa is (i minus 1)/2 rounded down; the loop stops when HK[pa] is at most HK[i]; otherwise HK[pa] and HK[i] are swapped, HV[pa] and HV[i] are swapped, and i becomes pa. `hpop()`: k is HK[0] and v is HV[0]; the last key lk and the last value lv are removed from the ends; when the heap is still not empty, HK[0] becomes lk and HV[0] becomes lv and, with i at 0, repeatedly: a is 2i+1, b is a plus 1 and m is i; m becomes a when a is below the heap length and HK[a] is below HK[m]; m becomes b when b is below the heap length and HK[b] is below HK[m]; the loop stops when m is i; otherwise entries m and i are swapped in both arrays and i becomes m; the popped key and value are k and v. While the heap is not empty: dv and i are popped; when dv is above DJ[i] nothing more happens for this entry; otherwise for each s from NA0[i] below NA0[i+1]: l is NAL[s], j is LB[l] when LA[l] is i, else LA[l]; L is `hypot3`(PMV[3i] minus PMV[3j], PMV[3i+1] minus PMV[3j+1], PMV[3i+2] minus PMV[3j+2]); hh is (HN[i] plus HN[j])/2; nd is dv plus L/(hh·hh); when nd is below DJ[j], DJ[j] becomes nd, LG[j] becomes LG[i] plus L, and nd with j is pushed. Then mx and ml start at 0.0 and, for each node i in order with DJ[i] finite, mx becomes `jmax`(mx, DJ[i]) and ml becomes `jmax`(ml, LG[i]); the row is node src, ecc mx and len ml. The rows are appended to `GRN` (node), `GRC` (ecc) and `GRL` (len), which are emptied first and then each get `reserve` of the number of picks; the rows are then sorted by ecc ascending with a stable insertion sort (a row moves before the previous one only while the previous ecc is above its ecc). `im_gates` reports views `im_view_i32` 85 `GRN`, `im_view_f64` 86 `GRC` and 87 `GRL`, and returns the number of rows.
